#X msg 130 592 apin_mapping?;
#X text 270 592 query mapping between analog port number and digital
pin. Analog messages are numbered 0 to 15 \, which traditionally refer
to the Arduino pins labeled A0 \, A1 \, A2 \, etc. However \, these
pis are actually configured using "normal" pin numbers in the pin mode
message \, and when those pins are used for non-analog functions. The
analog mapping query provides the information about which pins (as
used with Firmata's pin mode message) correspond to the analog channels.
Return sequence of messages like: [apin_mapping A# PIN#( \, where #
is number.;
#X msg 130 753 capabilities?;
#X text 270 753 query pin capabilities. Return sequence of messages
like: [pin_info PIN# MODE RESOLUTION( \, where # is pin number.;
#X msg 130 793 firmware?;
#X text 270 793 query firmata protocol version. Returns message like:
[firmware ARDUINO_FIRMWARE_NAME.ino MAJOR MINOR(.;
#X msg 130 833 pin_mode;
#X text 270 833 sets pin mode. Аргументы:;
#X obj 280 856 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 856 PIN#: pin number. Тип: int. Минимальное значение: 0\.;
#X obj 280 879 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 879 MODE: pin mode. Тип: symbol. Разрешённые значения:
INPUT \, OUTPUT \, ANALOG \, PWM \, SERVO \, SHIFT \, I2C \, ONEWIRE
\, STEPPER \, ENCODER \, SERIAL \, PULLUP.;
#X msg 130 934 pin_state?;
#X text 270 934 query pin state. The pin state is any data written
to the pin (it is important to note that pin state != pin value). For
output modes (digital output \, PWM \, and Servo) \, the state is any
value that has been previously written to the pin. For input modes
\, typically the state is zero. However \, for digital inputs \, the
state is the status of the pull-up resistor which is 1 if enabled \,
0 if disabled. Returns message like [pin_state PIN# MODE state( \,
where # is pin number. Аргументы:;
#X obj 280 1093 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1093 PIN#: pin number. Тип: int.;
#X msg 130 1118 report_apin;
#X text 270 1118 turns on/off analog pin (A0-A6) value reporting. Аргументы:;
#X obj 280 1141 cnv 1 83 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1141 ANALOG_PIN: analog pin number. Тип: int.;
#X obj 280 1164 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1164 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates analog reporting \,
messages like [apin PIN# value( are returned every sampling interval
(by default 19ms). Тип: int. Разрешённые значения: 0 \, 1\.;
#X msg 130 1219 report_dport;
#X text 270 1219 turns on/off digital port value reporting. Аргументы:;
#X obj 280 1242 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1242 PORT#: digital port number. Port is a group of pins
\, port 0 refers pins 0-8\. Тип: int.;
#X obj 280 1280 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1280 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates digital port reporting
\, messages like [dport PORT# value( are returned only on pin value
change. Тип: int. Разрешённые значения: 0 \, 1\.;
#X msg 130 1335 samp_interval;
#X text 270 1335 sets sampling interval - how often analog data and
i2c data is reported to the client. The default for the arduino implementation
is 19ms. This means that every 19ms analog data will be reported and
any i2c devices with read continuous mode will be read. Аргументы:;
#X obj 280 1434 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1434 TIME: time. Тип: int. Диапазон: 10…10000\. Единицы:
'ms'.;
